Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:38:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Electronic throttle turns back on by itself after a fault
 (pro-style)

New etbAutoRecoverEnabled (off by default), etbAutoRecoverDelay and
etbAutoRecoverMaxTries. After a latched intermittent TPS or pedal error, or a jam,
once both sensors read fine for the delay, the throttle is turned back on (jam rev
limit lifted too), up to the max number of times per power up. Fatal errors are never
cleared. Live data etbAutoRecoverCount. TS: in the ETB jam detection dialog.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TkhsyMr5ndz2MBCxuDZhPC
